# Cloudflare Pages _redirects — gstcalculator.me
# Enforces trailing slash on all URLs

# Blog posts
/blog/:slug  /blog/:slug/  301

# Top-level pages
/blog     /blog/     301
/privacy  /privacy/  301
/about    /about/    301
/contact  /contact/  301

# No 404 fallback rule here — Cloudflare Pages' _redirects only accepts
# status 200/301/302/303/307/308 on a rule; a "404" rule (tried twice before)
# is silently dropped, and requests fall through to the platform's own bare
# empty-body 404 instead. The real fallback lives in functions/_middleware.ts,
# which serves dist/404/index.html (built by scripts/prerender-routes.mjs)
# through the ASSETS binding when context.next() comes back 404 — that's the
# documented way to control the 404 response from Cloudflare Pages Functions.
